blurb: The South Portland School District hosted a community forum to address a projected
  $7.2 million budget shortfall for FY27. The administration presented several major
  cost-saving ideas, including the potential reconfiguration of elementary schools,
  to tackle the challenges of declining enrollment and rising operational costs.
